1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,442
Can you get through this page with only a
keyboard?

2
00:00:03,442 --> 00:00:05,996
Most people can't see the path focus
takes.

3
00:00:05,996 --> 00:00:07,031
So let's draw it.

4
00:00:08,411 --> 00:00:11,114
This is a demo store, broken on purpose.

5
00:00:11,114 --> 00:00:16,250
Every number is a stop on the keyboard
path, and every line shows where focus

6
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:16,926
goes next.

7
00:00:18,154 --> 00:00:18,531
Watch.

8
00:00:18,531 --> 00:00:21,858
Focus jumps to the footer first, then back
to the top.

9
00:00:21,858 --> 00:00:26,818
It vanishes into a closed menu you can't
see, and lands on buttons with no focus

10
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:27,760
outline at all.

11
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:35,066
Click any finding to jump straight to it.

12
00:00:35,066 --> 00:00:38,519
Each one maps to WCAG, and you can
download the full report.

13
00:00:39,545 --> 00:00:41,467
Now, the same page, fixed.

14
00:00:43,695 --> 00:00:44,560
Zero errors.

15
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:48,744
Focus follows the reading order, and every
stop is visible.

16
00:00:53,847 --> 00:00:54,718
Three lessons.

17
00:00:54,718 --> 00:00:56,336
Tab order follows the DOM.

18
00:00:56,336 --> 00:00:58,888
If it can take focus, it must be visible.

19
00:00:58,888 --> 00:01:02,373
And never remove the focus outline without
a replacement.

20
00:01:02,373 --> 00:01:03,991
It's free and open source.

21
00:01:03,991 --> 00:01:05,734
The link is in the comments.
